## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to handle production data quality issues during migration, enforce governance, and execute a safe rollback or delta-based fix under constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-database migration and cutover planning
- Data quality remediation and reconciliation
- Rollback strategy and risk assessment
- Governance, audit logging, and data masking

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation: reconcile deltas and validate integrity
async function reconcileAndValidate(src, dest, checkpoint) {
  const delta = await computeDelta(src, dest, checkpoint);
  if (delta.discrepancies.length > 0) {
    await applyCorrections(dest, delta);
    await validateIntegrity(dest, checkpoint);
  }
  return { status: 'validated', delta };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes ownership under pressure, bias-for-action with guardrails, and customer-first decision making when data signals risk.

## Key Concepts
- Ownership of a high-stakes feature
- Actionable rollout strategies with safe fallbacks
- Customer-obsession through measurable, segment-aware metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo code: feature flag gating for checkout redesign
const FEATURE_FLAG = getFlag('checkoutRedesign');
if (FEATURE_FLAG && isMobileUser()) {
  showNewCheckout();
} else {
  showOldCheckout();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design rollback instrumentation to ensure rapid detection?
- How would you communicate risk trade-offs to leadership without slowing progress?
